## 7. A Fabric Sourcing Checklist for Designers and Boutiques

Before ordering fabric for a wedding outfit or boutique collection, verify the following details.

### Fabric Composition

Confirm the fibre content rather than relying only on the fabric's trade name.

### Usable Width

Check the cutting width and whether decorative borders reduce usable material.

### Fabric Quantity

Calculate requirements according to the garment pattern, measurements, motif placement and cutting wastage.

### Colour Consistency

Compare the shade across the required length, particularly when buying from different rolls.

### Repeat Availability

For boutique production, confirm whether the same fabric can be reordered.

### Total Garment Cost

Include lining, trims, stitching, embroidery and finishing costs rather than comparing only the fabric price.

Fashion students and independent designers can use these checks to develop more accurate sourcing sheets.

